From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:22:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: take all the RAM the host's memory maximum allows

The kernel asked for a fixed 64 MiB at boot, so a machine the host gave
256 MiB still had 64, and Lua's constructs test ran it out of memory.
It now asks for the wasm32 maximum and, on failure, shrinks the request
by a 64th of itself (about 200 tries, at most 1.6% left unused) where it
shrank by one page, so RAM is whatever the host's memory limit admits.
---
 arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig | 2 +-
 arch/wasm/kernel/head.S                  | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig b/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
--- a/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
+++ b/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
@@ -34,4 +34,4 @@
 # CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_WARN_ONLY is not set
 # CONFIG_RCU_TRACE is not set
 # CONFIG_RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU is not set
-CONFIG_BOOT_MEM_PAGES=0x400
+CONFIG_BOOT_MEM_PAGES=0xFFFF
diff --git a/arch/wasm/kernel/head.S b/arch/wasm/kernel/head.S
--- a/arch/wasm/kernel/head.S
+++ b/arch/wasm/kernel/head.S
@@ -37,20 +37,24 @@
 	iLONG.sub
 	local.set 0
-	/* gmux: on failure, shrink the request and retry; stop at success or zero */
+	/* gmux: on failure, shrink the request by a 64th and retry; stop at success or zero */
 	block
 	loop
 		local.get 0
 		WASM_MEMORY_GROW /* iLONG new -> iLONG old_or_error. */
 		iLONG.const -1 /* -1 means allocation failed. */
 		iLONG.ne
 		br_if 1
 
 		local.get 0
+		local.get 0
+		iLONG.const 6
+		iLONG.shr_u
 		iLONG.const 1
+		iLONG.add
 		iLONG.sub
 		local.tee 0
 		iLONG.eqz
 		br_if 1
 		br 0
 	end_loop
 	end_block
-- 
2.43.0

